  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Colorado federal contract obligations total $108M for FY2027 to date. The federal government recorded 382 awards in the state, with an average award size of $283K. Obligations are down 99.2% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows year-to-year scale: FY22 was $14B, FY23 was $14.9B, FY24 was $15B, FY25 was $16.1B, FY26 was $14.4B, and FY27 is $108M to date. The Department of Homeland Security leads buying in FY2027 to date with $44.8M, followed by the General Services Administration with $23.4M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $13.9M. ARDENT GROUP, LLC is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date at $44.8M, followed by BLUESTAQ LLC at $24.3M and HSG PARK JOINT VENTURE 3, LLC at $7.5M. Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds is the largest listed industry at $44.8M, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $21.9M. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
