        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security accounts for the largest share of FY2027 to date obligations with $44.8M. The General Services Administration and the Department of Veterans Affairs follow with $23.4M and $13.9M respectively, showing a small set of agencies drive most current-year spending. Total obligations for FY2027 to date are $108M, so these top buyers represent a substantial portion of current-year activity."
      },
